    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Political consolidation of India primarily took place between 1947 and 1964.",
        "The Cold War geopolitical structure spanned from 1945 until 1991.",
        "The dissolution of the Soviet Union in 1991 marked a critical turning point in global and Indian foreign relations.",
        "India's development post-independence involves economic planning, constitutional foundations, nuclear policy, and social welfare developments."
      ],
      "id": "repzebj"
    },
    {
      "id": "nbwxs4r",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. POLITICAL CONSOLIDATION (1947–1964)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eaudm66",
      "content": "• Integration of Princely States under Sardar Patel."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "newdyxc",
      "content": "• Constitution of India came into force on 26 January 1950."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1460gsl",
      "content": "• Reorganization of States (1956) on linguistic basis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6vj14sr",
      "content": "• Adoption of Parliamentary democracy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kjhngo1",
      "content": "• First General Elections (1951–52)."
    },
    {
      "id": "7tzux23",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. ECONOMIC PLANNING & FIVE-YEAR PLANS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9nbf24w",
      "content": "• Planning Commission established (1950)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p42cezw",
      "content": "• First Five-Year Plan (1951–56) — Agriculture focus."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "apchc10",
      "content": "• Second Plan — Heavy industries (Mahalanobis model)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e5clngq",
      "content": "• Green Revolution (1960s) — Food grain self-sufficiency."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "655u2xh",
      "content": "• Nationalization of Banks (1969)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e9h0l9j",
      "content": "• LPG Reforms (1991) — Liberalization, Privatization, Globalization."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rgorpcc",
      "content": "• NITI Aayog replaced Planning Commission (2015)."
    },
    {
      "id": "e64e0fi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. INDIA AND THE COLD WAR"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5q1bvr0",
      "content": "• Cold War between USA and USSR after World War II."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bkdz2iu",
      "content": "• India adopted Non-Aligned Movement (NAM)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "83wyycl",
      "content": "• Founder leaders: Nehru (India), Tito (Yugoslavia), Nasser (Egypt)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8q3z7lm",
      "content": "• Close strategic ties developed with Soviet Union (1971 Treaty of Peace &amp; Friendship)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m07tj0j",
      "content": "• Indo-US relations improved after 2000 (Civil Nuclear Deal 2008)."
    },
    {
      "id": "d7ubjv2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. INDIA–SOVIET UNION RELATIONS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q4qy7o0",
      "content": "• USSR supported India in UN Security Council during 1971 Bangladesh War."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pvq77dl",
      "content": "• Cooperation in defence (MiG aircraft), space and heavy industries."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vl8ci0c",
      "content": "• Soviet Union dissolved in 1991; Russia continued partnership."
    },
    {
      "id": "p2iz16o",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. INDIA AND THE UNITED NATIONS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9jqovbc",
      "content": "• India is a founding member of the UN (1945).                 "
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tys848v",
      "content": "• Active participation in UN Peacekeeping Missions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "br6abjh",
      "content": "• Demand for permanent seat in UN Security Council."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "43ajf8y",
      "content": "• Leadership in decolonization and anti-apartheid movements."
    },
    {
